    f923_gas_price_plausibility_screen: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-49 (2026-09-08) \u2014 LANDED, default ON, on the SPP keeper's OWN measured footprint (zero LP, keeper-3 rebuilt fleet_only on the unedited and the repaired tree): 2024 \u2014 55 own-reporting plants, 642 plant-months, 60 low / 11 NEGATIVE / 25 high on 19 plants; 316 CT rows / 6.9 GW and 84 ST_GAS rows / 5.8 GW moved once the nearby pool is built from screened months (90 rows / 10.4 GW own-reported); 2023 34 high / 5 low; 2025 37 low / 5 negative / 6 high with 227 OK months on the US fallback (N3045OK3 unpublished for 2025). SPP-46's attribution reproduced pre-repair to the GWh (Pioneer +5,013; Harrington's ST_GAS fuel_low +6,136; ST_GAS clean \u22126,062 vs \u22125,949) and the repaired arrays move exactly those rows: Pioneer +5,013 \u2192 +1,650 (3.43 \u2192 9.0), CT fuel_low +8,963 \u2192 +3,223, ST_GAS fuel_low +6,136 \u2192 +1,493, clean cohorts within 0.6 TWh (FINDING-spp-49 \u00a70). Realised pooled re-clearing: 2024 CT \u22128.5 / ST \u22124.1 / CC +5.6 / COAL +6.6 TWh at +4.7 % level; 2025 CT \u22128.8; 2023 CT \u22123.6. Seam 2 clamps 21 rows / 1,142 MW (Pioneer 763). K = in the keeper's INPUT path by the ruling, not yet in a solved keeper: the re-baseline is SPP-50 (with SPP-48's wind repair in the same span). Harrington's fuel vintage (SPP-46 R-4) is untouched \u2014 the screen removes its $1.48 gas, not its coal. SOLVED BY SPP-50 (2026-09-08, FINDING-spp-50-2026-09-08.md): the batched re-baseline \u2014 this seam PLUS SPP-48's wind R-LEVEL repair, keeper-3's recipe otherwise byte for byte (0 diffs across 297 meta keys outside provenance, 0 across every scenario_config field present in both configs, all 8 shared-input fingerprints unmoved), full span in ONE invocation. The realised LP response reproduces the zero-LP pooled prediction on every class of every year: 2024 CT \u22128.06 TWh (predicted \u22128.46), CC_REGULAR +5.74 (+5.60), COAL +5.66 (+6.63), ST_GAS \u22123.60 (\u22124.14); 2025 CT \u22128.77 (\u22128.80), CC_REGULAR +2.29 (+2.29). C1 SUBSTANTIALLY REPAIRED \u2014 the two targeted 2024 rows FIXED (CC_REGULAR \u22128.60 \u2192 \u22122.94, CT_PEAKER +9.94 \u2192 +1.91), COAL_PRB \u22124.80 \u2192 +0.26, summed absolute class error 31.69 \u2192 16.45 TWh in 2024 and 22.91 \u2192 15.67 in 2023, free-class 10/12 \u2192 11/12; ONE new failing row, ST_GAS-2024 \u22125.12 \u2192 \u22128.71, root-caused to the already-routed Harrington fuel vintage. PRICE LEVEL WORSE IN EVERY YEAR, reported at full magnitude: C3a +14.1/+7.5/+7.2 \u2192 +15.0/+12.1/+14.2 % (2024 and 2025 flip PASS\u2192FAIL at the year level), C3b 2025 0.189 \u2192 0.253. Determination NOT-YET, the same four criteria and the same grade summary as keeper-3. The lane RECOMMENDS promotion on structural grounds (rule 1: keeper-3's better price level was produced by gas at $0.16/MMBtu, the unreal mechanism that rule forbids) and registered WITHOUT promoting \u2014 keepers/SPP.json UNTOUCHED, the promotion is card P15. K therefore still reads 'in the keeper's INPUT path by the ruling': the solved run exists and is registered as 2026-09-08-spp-50-rebaseline, but SPP's DESIGNATED keeper does not carry the seam until the owner rules." },
