    tranche_startup_amortization: { cell: "R", ev: "SPP MERIT-ORDER (2026-09-07) — R: REFUSED AT PHASE 0 ON ITS OWN ARITHMETIC, ZERO LP SPENT (rule 29 clause 0). Covers v2 tranche_startup_amortization + v3 tranche_startup_measured_runs, the arm as declared in PRECOMMIT-spp-merit-order-2026-09-07.md §3.1; v4 tranche_startup_conditional_runs was never part of it and is untested. ADMISSIBLE, then refused on size — the rule-19 [R-ONE-MECH] enumeration that REFUSED this mechanism on ERCOT (DIAGNOSIS-ercot145-tranche-startup-2026-07-31.md §1: ERCOT CT rows already carried +$13.1/+$34.9/+$292-451 of FITTED multiplier margin against a $2.9-4.0 measured amortization, i.e. stacking) points the OTHER WAY on SPP: every SPP band multiplier is 1.0, so the CT_PEAKER/CT_CHP econ+peak and CC_* peak rows carry an above-SRMC margin of exactly $0.00 — ERCOT-145's own \"four keeper ISOs\" regime. Rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]: SPP's OWN artifact derived and committed by this lane, data/raw/_processed-legacy/campd_ct_run_lengths_SPP.csv (scripts/data/derive_campd_ct_run_lengths.py --iso SPP; 51 facilities / 138 units / 50,460 measured start-to-stop runs, 2023-2025, class-fallback median 9.0 h, per-plant p25 7 / p50 9 / p75 11 h) — SPP CTs run LONGER than every other ISO's measured fleet (NYISO 4, CAISO 4, ERCOT 6, PJM 7, MISO 10 h), which is why the measured markup is small. FOOTPRINT (arm fleet_only rebuild, mc_base byte-identical to the control): 384 rows / 11,600.3-11,630.9 MW gain a start-recovery term — CT_PEAKER econ+peak 10,519-10,566 MW at $20/MW-start over 9 h = MAX $2.140-2.141/MWh cap-weighted, CT_CHP 116-132 MW at $0.66-0.87, CC/CC_CHP peak 949 MW on the v2 P0 basis. GATE G-ROT (threshold INHERITED UNCHANGED from the price-family lane's pre-registered G-2: the steepening ratio MHR(>95pct)/MHR(25-75pct) must RISE >= 10 % of the control): at the arm's MAXIMUM markup the ratio moves 1.5653 -> 1.5676 (+0.147 %), 1.3306 -> 1.3396 (+0.676 %), 1.6665 -> 1.6833 (+1.008 %) in 2023/2024/2025 — a STOP by 10-68x — while the level moves the WRONG WAY (LW mean x1.0230 / x1.0228 / x1.0188 on a model already too dear). Granting the un-computable CC-peak leg a generous 9 h (or punitive 4 h) horizon turns rotation NEGATIVE in two of three years (-0.588/-0.135/+0.696 %; -0.952/-0.443/+2.016 %), so the refusal is robust to that limitation, not dependent on it. Graded on a re-clearing predictor VALIDATED against the price-family lane's SOLVED 2025 arm (LP-measured LW -9.05 % vs predicted -8.11/-9.12 %; LP-measured rotation +0.52 % vs predicted +2.09 %, i.e. the instrument OVER-STATES rotation ~4x — reported against interest, and it can only make the gate easier). No LP, no bundle, no registration; keeper 2026-09-07-spp-3-screened-input unchanged. Record: docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-merit-order-2026-09-07.md §4.2." },
    measured_ct_heat_rates: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7. SPP-46 (2026-09-07, zero LP): NAMED beside a CT physical-floor analogue of EGRID_CC_HR_PHYSICAL_CEILING as the repair for Pioneer 57881 (Basin Electric, ND): eGRID PLHTRT 3.43 MMBtu/MWh on simple-cycle GTs (EIA-923 gen ~3x its CAMPD gross load) makes it a $12/MWh baseload row — model in-merit 5.6 TWh/yr against 0.5–0.6 measured, +5.0 TWh of the 2024 CT over-run on one plant; the fleet rows also sum to 763 MW against a 427 MW nameplate. Still U: no SPP artifact. ROUTED SPP-46 R-2." },
